# Claim C4, third manifestation -- FIXED 2026-08-26 by the
# template-clone isolation change (ADR-005): with the type()d alias
# pair at the TOP LEVEL of the included file, the pattern now emits
# the record. Historically it died with a bogus
# [aontu/mapval_spread_required] "The value for key T is required
# (defined in spread)" though NO spread existed in either file: the
# include's root-map meet wrapped the resolved, type-marked alias as
# an EXPECTATION (a non-genable peer-only child), and the wrapper
# carried no mark for gen to skip. A marked peer child is now carried,
# never expected (BagVal.handleExpectedVal / expectGenable).
# Pinned in both engines: test/spec/file.tsv load-alias-top-conjunct.
# expected: {"customers":{"c1":{"a":5}}} exit 0
# actual:   {"customers":{"c1":{"a":5}}} exit 0
@"./alias-top.aon"
customers: c1: $.C & { a: 5 }
